      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d0800ed67a32f0e119a70dd|full_name}: I'd say in this case, this is less about feature parity anyways since VRChat is essentially blocking the system keyboard and *reimplementing* their own, which is more limited.\nIn this case, I feel like implemeneting input methods is \"out of scope\" beyond defining which input methods are supported.\nThough I understand on PC this would be more difficult as searching seems to suggest Valve discontinued the SteamVR Keyboard API ages ago, and I do understand the desire to maintain consistency.\nAt the very least, I feel like it should be optional; Perhaps in settings there could be a \"Enabled Keyboard Overlay\" checkbox with a tooltip that explains the on-screen keyboard will be replaced with the Oculus Keyboard Overlay?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
